@ 42.1.1.1.1 - Proto-Finnish to Standard Finnish
# citation: Tropylium, from Hakulinen, Lauri (1979), “Suomen kielen rakenne ja kehitys”. Otava; Häkkinen, Kaisa (2004), “Nykysuomen etymologinen sanakirja”. WSOY; Kallio, Petri (2007), “Kantasuomen konsonanttihistoriaa”. Mémoires de la Société Finno-Ougrienne 253.
	{ mb, nd, ŋɡ } > { m:[+long], n:[+long], ŋ:[+long] }
	{ e:[+long], ø:[+long], o:[+long] } > { ie, yø, uo }
	{ pˑ, tˑ, θˑ, kˑ } > { p, t, θ, k }
	j > i / C_, when initial in a suffix
	Vh > hV / :{ j_# (also some double-metathesis triggered by the condition of being m_ ?), v_# (also some double-metathesis triggered by the condition of being m_ ?), n_# (also some double-metathesis triggered by the condition of being m_ ?), r_# (also some double-metathesis triggered by the condition of being m_ ?), l_# (also some double-metathesis triggered by the condition of being m_ ?) }:
	sn > ns
	V > V:[+long] / h_hC
	V > V:[+long] / _hC (sporadic)
	{k,x} > ˟ / _#
	t > ∅ / s_r
	p > β / _S
	β > % / _S
	t > z / _r{[+affricate],O}
	z > % / _r{[+affricate],O}
	t > z / _r{i,e}
	z > @ / _r{i,e}
	k > z / _j
	z > @ / _j
	k > ɣ i / :{ i_S{i,e}, e_S{i,e} }:
	k > ɣ / :{ [+affricate]_S, O_S, %_S }: // S = j
	ɣ > % / :{ [+affricate]_S, O_S, %_S }: // S = j
	β > ʋ
	ʋ > ∅ / _%C
	ið > j / V_V
	{ lð, rð } > { l:[+long], r:[+long] }
	ð > ∅ // V(X)_
	ɣ > j / C_e
	ɣ > ʋ / %_%
	ɣ > ʔ / VV_V // V = %
	ɣ > ∅
	h > ∅ / V:[-stress](X)_V
	[+affricate]O > {[+affricate],O,%}:[+long] / unstressed
	e > i / [+affricate]_, when unstressed
	%e > e:[+long] / unstressed
	V% > V:[+long] / _#
	{ i%, O% } > { %:[+long], O:[+long] }
	æ > a / e(C…)_(C…)o
	e > ø / #(C…)_y
	i > y / #(C…)l_y
	i > y / #(C…)_væ
	{ θ, θ:[+long] } ð > t͡s d (this latter does have some highly sporadic exceptions; additionally, in some dialect͡s these may become {{ t, t:[+long] },h~t} and {r,∅}, respectively)